cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Shoalscope, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
title: "Shoalscope: fish monitoring with scientific echosounders"
abstract: >-
  Shoalscope turns raw split-beam echosounder data into fish targets, tracks, passage counts,
  densities, school catalogues and diel-migration metrics with physics-based, rule-based methods
  (calibrated sonar equations, published noise removal, split-beam single-target detection,
  Kalman tracking and echo integration). It reads public observatory and survey archives through
  index-guided byte ranges and stores versioned, traceable products in an Icechunk and Apache
  Iceberg lakehouse.
authors:
  - family-names: Mohammadpour
    given-names: Soheil
repository-code: https://github.com/soheil-mp/shoalscope
license: MIT
version: 0.0.0
keywords:
  - fisheries acoustics
  - echosounder
  - sonar
  - fish
  - target tracking
  - echo integration
  - data engineering
